        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: точка зрения",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "точка зрения (tóchka zréniya) — \"a point of view\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "С моей точки зрения, это хорошая идея. S moyéy tóchki zréniya, éto khoróshaya idéya. From my point of view, it is a good idea."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Feminine, after точка: genitive точки зрения. С моей точки зрения — from my point of view."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "точка is usually traced to the verb ткнуть \"to poke, to jab\": a dot is the mark a jab leaves (EtymDB lists Lithuanian taškas \"a dot\" beside it). зрение \"sight\" is built on the old verb зреть \"to look\", so a point of view is literally the point you look from."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
            }
          ]
        },
