          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: позиция",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "позиция (pozítsiya) — \"a position, a stance\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Моя позиция проста: надо больше читать. Moyá pozítsiya prostá: nádo bólshe chitát. My position is simple: we need to read more."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Feminine. Занимать позицию — to take a position. It is also a place in a list or a team: первая позиция (pozítsiya)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "позиция (pozítsiya) is usually traced, through western European languages, to Latin positiō \"a placing, a position\" (Lewis & Short), which is built on pōnere \"to put, to place\". A stance is where you have placed yourself."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
