              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "взгляд (vzglyad) — \"a view, an opinion; a look\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "У нас разные взгляды на жизнь. U nas ráznyye vzglyády na zhizn. We have different views on life."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine. На мой взгляд (vzglyad) — in my view. It is also a glance: быстрый взгляд (vzglyad)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "взгляд (vzglyad) is inherited from Proto-Slavic vŭzględŭ (EtymDB), built from the prefix vŭz- \"up\" and ględěti \"to look\", the verb that survives in глядеть. A view began as a look upwards."
