          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "заявлять (zayavlyát) — \"to declare, to state publicly\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Директор заявляет, что завод не закроют. Diréktor zayavlyáyet, chto zavód ne zakróyut. The director states that the factory will not be closed."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Imperfective; perfective заявить (заявлю, заявишь). Formal: officials and newspapers заявляют, while among friends people говорят."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "заявлять (zayavlyát) is built from за- and являть \"to show, to reveal\", the verb behind явный \"obvious\". Явить comes through Old East Slavic javiti from Proto-Slavic aviti \"to make visible\" (EtymDB): to declare is to make a thing plain."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
