          "title": "You'll want to know: считаться",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "считаться (schitátsya) — \"to be considered, to be regarded as\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Этот район считается самым тихим в городе. Étot rayón schitáyetsya sámym tíkhim v górode. This district is considered the quietest in the city."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "An imperfective verb. It takes the instrumental: считается лучшим. Считаться с + instrumental — to take into account."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "считаться (schitátsya) is the reflexive of считать, built from с- and читать. Читать shares its root with число \"number\", from Proto-Slavic čislo, built on čisti (EtymDB): to be considered is to be counted as something."
            }
          ]
        },
